---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { business } from "../data/site";

const updated = "September 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms"
  description="The terms that apply to using the Top Order Digital website and engaging Simon to build a website."
  stickyCta={false}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Terms</span>
      <h1 style="margin-top:1.25rem">Terms</h1>
      <p class="prose__updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p>
        {business.name} is {business.owner}, a sole trader (ABN {business.abn})
        based in {business.suburb}. These terms cover two things: using this
        website, and what you can expect if you engage me to build one for you.
      </p>

      <h2>Using this website</h2>
      <p>
        The information on {business.domain} — the price range, timeframes and
        what's included in the package — is provided in good faith and kept
        current, but it's a starting point, not a fixed quote. Your quote is
        whatever I confirm to you in writing by email.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site's design, text, code and logo are mine or licensed to me.
        Please don't copy them for your own use without asking.
      </p>

      <h2>If I build your website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Quote and scope.</strong> I'll email you a plain-English
          summary of what I'll build and the price before any work starts.
          That's what we're both agreeing to.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Payment.</strong> A deposit of $250–400 is due before work
          starts, and the balance of the build price is due when the site goes
          live. I'll confirm the exact figure in writing first.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What's in the build price.</strong> A custom site of up to
          five pages, your domain registered for two years, and twelve months of
          managed hosting from the day the site goes live.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Revisions.</strong> Unlimited revisions before go-live, within
          the agreed scope. New pages or work beyond that scope are quoted
          separately and only start once you've agreed to them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>What I need from you.</strong> Your content, photos, logo,
          ABN and any licence details, and prompt answers to my questions. If
          these are slow to arrive, the timeframe moves with them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Timeframe.</strong> Two weeks is typical once I have what I
          need. I'll tell you early if anything's going to push that out.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Ownership.</strong> When the build is paid for, the website,
          its files and the domain are yours outright. Nothing sits on a
          reseller platform, and there is nothing to buy back from me.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Hosting after the first year.</strong> Twelve months after
          go-live, hosting continues at $49 per month. I'll email you before it
          starts. You can cancel at any point, and I'll help you move the site
          and domain to another host if you'd prefer.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        I'll build your site with reasonable care and skill. Nothing in these
        terms limits rights you have under the Australian Consumer Law. Beyond
        those rights, I'm not liable for indirect or consequential loss, and my
        total liability for any claim is limited to the amount you've paid me
        for the work it relates to.
      </p>
      <p>
        I can't guarantee specific search rankings or enquiry numbers — those
        depend on your market, your reviews and factors outside my control. What
        I guarantee is a fast, well-built site set up properly for local search.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the law of Western Australia.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> and I'll
        talk you through any of it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
